How steamcards farms trading cards follows ArchiSteamFarm
(https://github.com/JustArchiNET/ArchiSteamFarm), Copyright 2015-2026
Łukasz "JustArchi" Domeradzki, licensed under the Apache License 2.0:
the badge-page selectors (library/steam-api/src/badges.rs), what an
inventory item's tags say it is (library/steam-api/src/inventory.rs), the
farming rules and timings (component/farming/domain/src/rules.rs), including
its list of sale-event app IDs, and the hours its time to finish adds for
games short of their hours (component/farming/domain/src/forecast.rs). They
were rewritten in Rust for steamcards; no ASF source code is included.

Steam's message definitions follow Valve's own .proto files, as published by
SteamDatabase (https://github.com/SteamDatabase/Protobufs).
